    "detail": "Our own addition (no UAT item or ticket asks for axe): record-only, findings are suggestions. Spec newspec-c/vis-tc06-s21-s22-badge-visual.spec.ts ran axe-core 4.14 (WCAG 2 A/AA) on six screens (hospital-chart-preround, hospital-chart-encounter, hospital-add, nh-chart-preround, nh-chart-encounter, and /snf/add, which the visual lane never captured) on desktop Chromium 1280x800, Pixel 7 Chromium and iPhone 15 WebKit (18 captures, fresh @roundai.test account, no model). The three controls the scenario names are clean on every screen and profile: the status select is named 'Admission status' (4 chart screens x 3 profiles), the Note Format picker is named 'Note Format' (Hospital: H&P / SOAP progress / Consult note / Discharge summary; Nursing Home: SNF admission / SNF follow-up), both add forms' Encounter Type select is named by its label, and axe reports no violation on any of them. Other axe violations on these screens, identical on all three profiles: color-contrast (serious) on 5 of 6 screens (1-16 nodes: section headings, hints, a 10 px button on the Hospital Encounter tab; A4) and button-name (critical) on the Nursing Home chart's back arrow on both NH chart screens (A1, known). So 'no WCAG 2 A/AA violations on the listed screens' does not hold, but every violation is a known suggestion (A1/A4), none is on the named controls.",
